Section F: gizmo mathematics and undo/redo participation
  OK   world-space handles ignore the object's rotation
  OK   local-space handles follow the object's rotation (local X of a 90-degree yaw is world -Z)
  OK   scale handles are always the object's local axes
  OK   a ray at the X handle picks X
  OK   a ray at the Y handle picks Y
  OK   a ray far from every handle picks nothing
  OK   a ray on the Y ring (away from the other rings) picks the Y rotation handle
  OK   a ray on the X ring picks the X rotation handle
  OK   a translate drag begins from a ray on the axis
  OK   dragging 3 m along the X handle moves exactly 3 m along X and nothing else
  OK   snapping rounds the 2.7 m delta to 2.5 m (0.5 m steps from the start)
  OK   snap rounds to the nearest step
  OK   a rotate drag begins from a ray on the Y ring
  OK   dragging a quarter turn around Y rotates the object's X axis to -Z and leaves the position alone
  OK   rotation snapping rounds a 14-degree drag to 15 degrees
  OK   a scale drag begins from a ray on the Y handle
  OK   dragging half a handle length along Y adds 0.5 to the Y scale only
  OK   a ten-frame drag lands at 4 m and records one undo step
  OK   undo restores the pre-drag transform in one step
  OK   redo reapplies the whole drag
  OK   a cancelled edit records nothing
